# Medplum Repository Guidance

- This is a full-stack TypeScript monorepo using npm workspaces and Turbo. Prefer package-local patterns before adding shared abstractions.
- `packages/app` is the Medplum web app built with React, Vite, Mantine, React Router, and `@medplum/react`.
- `packages/server` is the Express API server backed by PostgreSQL and Redis, with OpenTelemetry instrumentation and migration scripts.
- FHIR and healthcare contracts are central. Treat resource schemas, search parameters, auth scopes, package exports, generated definitions, and API behavior as public contracts unless local context proves otherwise.
- Shared libraries such as `packages/core`, `packages/fhirtypes`, `packages/definitions`, `packages/react`, and `packages/react-hooks` can affect downstream packages and examples.
- Prefer targeted workspace commands first, for example `npm run test --workspace=@medplum/core`, `npm run test --workspace=@medplum/app`, or `npm run lint --workspace=@medplum/server`.
- Use root `npm test`, `npm run lint`, or `npm run build` only when the change crosses package boundaries or targeted checks are insufficient.

## Medplum Test Preflight

- Fresh agents may need `npm install` before any test command; check that the runner exists before retrying failures.
- App and server Jest tests can require built workspace `dist` artifacts such as `packages/core/dist`, `packages/react/dist`, `packages/mock/dist`, and `packages/fhir-router/dist`.
- If those artifacts are missing, run `npm run build:fast` before app/server Jest tests.
- Server tests require Postgres and Redis. Check `localhost:5432`, `localhost:6379`, or Docker availability before running them; if services cannot be started, report the backend test as environment-blocked with the exact command to run later.
